(5)
The imposed loads must not be reduced in relation to—
(a)
floors of a building that support the equipment, machinery or displaying items referred to in section 7(3);
(b)
floors of factories and workshops designed for a distributed imposed load of less than 7.5 kPa;
(c)
floors used by vehicles;
(d)
office areas used for storage and filing purposes;
(e)
forces produced by dynamic effects;
(f)
floors used for storage purposes; or
(g)
loads from partitions the positions of which are not indicated on the plan of the building.
